{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1920,
 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why are there ships buried under San Francisco's skyscrapers?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.101
  },
  {
   "text": "Workers dig a hole for a new tower, and hit the bow of a wooden ship.",
   "s": 3.401,
   "e": 6.645
  },
  {
   "text": "Then another. And another. Dozens of ships, buried under downtown.",
   "s": 6.845,
   "e": 9.926
  },
  {
   "text": "It started in 1849, when someone found gold in the hills.",
   "s": 10.126,
   "e": 13.624
  },
  {
   "text": "Ships raced into the bay, and the moment they docked, everyone aboard ran for the gold.",
   "s": 13.824,
   "e": 18.034
  },
  {
   "text": "The sailors. The cooks. Even the captains.",
   "s": 18.234,
   "e": 20.04
  },
  {
   "text": "Soon, hundreds of empty ships rot in the harbor, a forest of masts with nobody home.",
   "s": 20.24,
   "e": 24.775
  },
  {
   "text": "People laugh: the busiest port in America, and not one ship can leave.",
   "s": 24.975,
   "e": 28.546
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it gets weirder. The town is so crowded, people move into the ships.",
   "s": 28.746,
   "e": 32.098
  },
  {
   "text": "One ship becomes a hotel. Another, a store. One becomes the town jail.",
   "s": 32.298,
   "e": 36.101
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a giant fire sweeps the waterfront, and the ships burn down to the waterline.",
   "s": 36.301,
   "e": 40.379
  },
  {
   "text": "So why are they underground now?",
   "s": 40.779,
   "e": 42.04
  },
  {
   "text": "Because the city wanted more land, so it dumped whole hills of dirt into the bay, right on top of the ships.",
   "s": 42.34,
   "e": 47.706
  },
  {
   "text": "Streets, banks and skyscrapers rise over them, and everyone forgets.",
   "s": 47.906,
   "e": 51.078
  },
  {
   "text": "Until a digger hits one again, still full of old bottles and boots.",
   "s": 51.278,
   "e": 54.532
  },
  {
   "text": "Today, trains even run straight through one buried ship's hull.",
   "s": 54.732,
   "e": 57.646
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow for a weird story every day. And next time you're downtown, look down.",
   "s": 57.846,
   "e": 62.129
  }
 ],
